seeker: now try to represent this "????" german flag by only using css. the top line in that tricolor flag is black, central is red and bottom one is orange or yellow.
supporter: Sure, I can provide an example of how to create the German flag using CSS. Here's an example implementation:

HTML:
```
<div class="flag-germany">
  <div class="flag-stripe flag-black"></div>
  <div class="flag-stripe flag-red"></div>
  <div class="flag-stripe flag-goldenrod"></div>
</div>
```

CSS:
```
.flag-germany {
  width: 200px;
  height: 133.33px;
}

.flag-stripe {
  height: 33.33%;
}

.flag-black {
  background-color: black;
}

.flag-red {
  background-color: red;
}

.flag-goldenrod {
  background-color: goldenrod;
}
```

The `flag-germany` class is the main wrapper for the flag, with a width-to-height ratio of 3:2, which is the same as the German national flag. The `flag-stripe` class is used for the stripes that make up the flag. And the `flag-black`, `flag-red`, and `flag-goldenrod` classes are used to set the color for each stripe.

This example implementation uses CSS properties like `width`, `height`, `background-color`, and `height` to style the different stripes. You can adjust the size and color of each stripe to suit your needs. Also, note that this implementation is just one of many possible ways to create the German flag using CSS.
